Held object: {bag / helmet / vinyl / bouquet / etc.}
Accent color: {color}
Aspect ratio: 9:16

Create a bold editorial poster combining realistic photography, oversized typography, and connected forced perspective.

The person must physically hold or control the foreground object. Keep one continuous, believable perspective chain:

body → shoulder → arm → wrist → hand → grip point → object.

The same object being held should extend naturally toward the camera and appear oversized only because it is very close to the lens. Do not place a separate oversized object in the foreground.

Use a low-angle wide-lens perspective with the person slightly farther back and the hand/object closest to camera. Keep the grip, fingers, arm, and object physically connected and anatomically correct.

Place a huge condensed sans-serif keyword behind the person, partially covered by the body, arm, and object to create real depth.

Add small editorial information around the edges using meaningful brand, event, product, date, location, or specification details.

Use a warm off-white paper background, subtle print grain, mostly black typography, and one restrained accent color.

Keep the composition clean, fashion-forward, realistic, and dimensional.

Prompt:

SUBJECT: {adult subject + identity}
OUTFIT: {outfit}
SCENE: {night location}
EXPRESSION: {mood}
COLOR PALETTE: {colors}
ASPECT RATIO: {9:16}

Create a realistic ultra-close night fashion portrait with an “almost collision” POV.

The adult subject is genuinely walking toward the photographer while the photographer backs away. Capture a real mid-step moment, with natural shoulder rotation, walking inertia, and the body still moving forward. The subject is already so close that another half-step would require them to move aside.

Use an 18–22mm full-frame-equivalent wide-angle lens, about 30–45 cm from the nearest shoulder and upper torso. Keep the camera only slightly above eye level with a gentle 7–15° downward angle.

Aim the optical axis around the clavicle and sternum rather than the face. Let the upper torso sit near the center of the frame, with the face slightly higher and the waist, hips, and upper thighs receding naturally.

Add a subtle fisheye-like character: mild barrel distortion, gentle central bulging, and slight peripheral stretching. Keep it controlled and photographic — no extreme fisheye or GoPro distortion.

The near-collision feeling must come from torso-to-camera distance, not from reaching toward the lens. Keep both hands beside the body in natural walking motion.

Use strong direct flash to freeze the subject sharply against a darker night environment. Preserve realistic skin pores, natural texture, real hair strands, flyaways, believable fabric, and small motion traces in hair or clothing.

Use a different adult face for every new image while keeping the same camera language.

Tight head-to-upper-thigh framing, minimal empty space, slightly imperfect composition, strong physical proximity, and the feeling that the subject is one step away from bumping into the camera.

Avoid static poses, giant foreground hands, repeated faces, extreme top-down angles, extreme fisheye, distorted anatomy, plastic skin, oily highlights, CGI rendering, excessive neon, and studio lookbook styling.

Sky on full display.

Prompt: **Using my photo, create a photo**  
Create a selfie photo in the style of aesthetic summer photography. In the foreground is a young woman with long, thick, dark hair that flutters spectacularly in the wind. She holds a smartphone in her hand with a dark case decorated with a pattern (for example, with the image of stars or the moon), and takes a selfie from the bottom up.

**Details of appearance and make-up:**  
expressive eyes with long eyelashes, well-defined eyebrows;  
light but noticeable makeup: highlighter on cheekbones and nose, light blush;  
the lips are covered with gloss or lipstick of a delicate pink shade.;  
neat, well-groomed nails (the color of the varnish is at your discretion, but neutral or pastel is better).

**Clothing:**  
light-colored top with thin straps, slightly unbuttoned, with a soft texture (for example, knitwear or cotton);  
clothes should emphasize the lightness and ease of the image, be comfortable for walking in the fresh air.

**Posture and facial expression:**  
the woman tilts her head back slightly, looks at the camera with a slight half-smile or a neutral, calm expression.;  
the hair dynamically flutters in one direction, creating a feeling of a light breeze.;  
the hand with the phone is raised, the frame is taken from the bottom up — this visually lengthens the figure and adds drama.

**Background:**  
bright blue sky with fluffy white clouds, occupying most of the frame;  
The background should be clean, without unnecessary details, to draw attention to the model.;  
clouds should be voluminous, with soft edges that create a sense of depth and spaciousness.

**Lighting:**  
sunlight falling from above creates soft shadows on the face and clothes;  
high contrast and color saturation to enhance the brightness of the scene.

**Composition:**  
the framing is dense, with an emphasis on the face and upper body;  
slight asymmetry in the position of the head and phone for a modern, dynamic effect;  
hair and clouds should intertwine in the frame, creating a harmonious composition.

**The general mood:**  
lightness, freedom, the feeling of a carefree summer day;  
The aesthetics of the frame should combine naturalness and stylish presentation, be close to popular Instagram formats.;  
The emphasis is on the harmony between the model and the natural background, on the play of light and hair movement.

**Photo 9:16**

